# Locate Issues Precisely

When reporting bugs, gaps, or review findings, every issue must include a concrete code location. Vague section titles alone are not enough.

## Required format per finding

1. **Short title** of the problem
2. **Where** — `path` plus line range (use the real lines from the file)
3. **What** — one or two sentences on the bug/behavior
4. **Fix** — concrete suggestion

Prefer Cursor code citations:

```startLine:endLine:path/to/file
// relevant snippet
```

## Example (good)

**Promise.all treats missing open game as total failure**

```87:99:Frontend/Daily_flip/Src/Context/GameContext.tsx
const [openRes, currentRes] = await Promise.all([
  getOpenGame(),
  getCurrentGames(),
]);
// ...
} catch (err) {
  setHasJoined(false);
}
```

`GET /game/open` 404 fails the whole batch, so `/game/current` success is discarded. Fetch separately (or treat 404 as no live game).

## Example (bad)

> Gaps in GameContext: Promise.all fails if there’s no open game. Also currentGames not updated after join. Duplicate fetches.

No paths, no lines — do not write reviews this way.

## Also apply when

- Explaining why something breaks
- Listing multiple issues (each gets its own path + lines)
- Suggesting a refactor (point at the exact effect/function to change)
